#--: Overview

The declarations themselves live in #~"lib/system/ascii.z", which is the one
place they are written, each with its doc comment. This page is the prose.

#~"ascii" names the ASCII bytes that a character literal cannot spell. A
character literal is one identifier token that starts with #~"0c", so it
writes any byte an identifier may hold -- #~"0cA", #~"0c/", #~"0c_" -- and the
escapes #~"0c\\n", #~"0c\\t", #~"0c\\b", #~"0c\\\\" and #~"0c\\x20". The space and
the delimiters end an identifier, and most control bytes have no escape.
Those bytes have a name here. Each name is a #~"u8" constant.

The unit also holds the tests a program asks of a byte: whether it is a
digit, a letter, part of a name, white space.


#--: Index

#ul:
  [#*: #~"nul" 0, #~"bs" 8, #~"ht" 9, #~"lf" 10, #~"cr" 13, #~"del" 127 -- the
    control bytes, under their ASCII mnemonics]
  [#*: #~"space" 32]
  [#*: #~"doubleQuote" 34, #~"hash" 35, #~"backtick" 96]
  [#*: #~"parenOpen" 40, #~"parenClose" 41, #~"bracketOpen" 91,
    #~"bracketClose" 93, #~"braceOpen" 123, #~"braceClose" 125]
  [#*: #~"comma" 44, #~"dot" 46, #~"colon" 58, #~"semicolon" 59]
  [#*: #~"isDigit" / #~"isHexDigit" -- #~"function {b: u8} out bool":
    #~"0" to #~"9"; those and #~"a" to #~"f" in either case]
  [#*: #~"isUpper" / #~"isLower" / #~"isLetter" -- #~"A" to #~"Z";
    #~"a" to #~"z"; either]
  [#*: #~"isWord" -- a letter, a digit or #~"_": a byte of a name]
  [#*: #~"isSpace" / #~"isBlank" -- the space, the tab, the line feed or
    the carriage return; the space or the tab]


#--: Which spelling to write

#ul:
  [#*: A byte an identifier may hold is a character literal: #~"0c/",
    #~"0c0", #~"0c_".]
  [#*: A control byte that has an escape is that escape: #~"0c\\n",
    #~"0c\\t". The others are named: #~"ascii.cr", #~"ascii.nul".]
  [#*: The space and a delimiter are named: #~"ascii.space",
    #~"ascii.comma", #~"ascii.braceOpen".]
  [#*: A byte that is only appended to a text is written as text:
    #~"buf.append \",\"".]

#code language=zerolang: """
  # count the fields of one comma-separated line
  fields: function {line: StringView} out u64 is {
      n: 1.u64
      for each b: line.byteView loop {
          if b == ascii.comma then n = n + 1
      }
      return n
  }

  main: function is {
      print "\{fields line: "a,b,c"}"   # 3
  }
  """

A test takes the byte as #~"b":

#code language=zerolang: """
  # the digits of `s`, as a number
  digitsOf: function {s: StringView} out u64 is {
      n: 0.u64
      for each b: s.byteView loop {
          if (ascii.isDigit :b) then n = n * 10 + (b - 0c0).u64
      }
      return n
  }

  main: function is {
      print "\{digitsOf s: "a1b22"}"   # 122
  }
  """
